 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Programs make decisions with conditions.\n• “if <condition> then …” runs blocks only when the condition is true.\n• “if <condition> then … else …” chooses between two sets of blocks.\n• Conditions use comparison operators: = (equal), > (greater than), < (less than); and logic operators: and, or, not.\n• Sensing blocks test things: “touching edge?”, “key space pressed?”, “answer” from “ask … and wait”.\n• Operator blocks do arithmetic: +, −, ×, ÷, and “pick random 1 to 10”.\nExample: ask “How old are you?” and wait; if answer > 12 then say “Secondary school” else say “Primary school”.\nDebugging is finding and fixing errors (bugs) in a program; test it with different inputs.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "x": 15,
   "l": 10
  },
  "problem": "A program does: if x > {l} then say “big” else say “small”. What does it say when x = {x}?",
  "steps": [
   "Test the condition: is {x} > {l}?",
   "Yes, it is true, so the “then” part runs."
  ],
  "answer": "{traceIf(x, l, 'big', 'small')}",
  "checks": []
 },
